# SEO

Full technical SEO rules for `apps/web` (personal portfolio, mostly static) and `apps/blog` (software development blog). Both apps are deployed on separate domains — `yourdomain.com` and `blog.yourdomain.com`. All content is in Spanish.

> **Never apply these rules to `apps/admin`**. The admin panel must always have `robots: { index: false, follow: false }`.

---

## 1. Environment constants

Each app exposes its production URL through an environment variable. Use it everywhere an absolute URL is constructed.

```
# apps/web/.env.local / .env.production
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://yourdomain.com

# apps/blog/.env.local / .env.production
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://blog.yourdomain.com
```

---

## 2. `metadataBase` and global title — RootLayout

`metadataBase` is required for Next.js to correctly resolve relative URLs in Open Graph, Twitter, and canonical tags. It must be defined **once** in each app's root layout.

### apps/web — `app/layout.tsx`

```tsx
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  metadataBase: new URL(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL!),
  title: {
    default: 'Your Name · Software Developer',
    template: '%s · Your Name',
  },
  description: 'Personal portfolio of Your Name, software developer focused on...',
  authors: [{ name: 'Your Name', url: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL }],
  creator: 'Your Name',
  openGraph: {
    type: 'website',
    locale: 'es_ES',           // content is in Spanish — keep as-is
    siteName: 'Your Name · Portfolio',
    url: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL,
  },
  twitter: {
    card: 'summary_large_image',
    site: '@yourtwitter',      // replace with your real handle (or remove if unused)
    creator: '@yourtwitter',
  },
  robots: { index: true, follow: true },
};

export default function RootLayout({ children }: ...): React.JSX.Element {
  return (
    <html lang="es">           {/* always "es" — content is in Spanish */}
      ...
    </html>
  );
}
```

### apps/blog — `app/layout.tsx`

```tsx
