## 7. Images — `next/image`

All images **must** use `next/image`. Never use a native `<img>` tag.

### Required rules

| Prop | Rule |
|------|------|
| `alt` | Always present. Descriptive of the content. Use `alt=""` only for purely decorative images. |
| `width` + `height` | Always explicit for fixed-size images. Prevents CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift). |
| `fill` | Use with `sizes` when the container is relative-positioned. Always wrap in a `div` with `position: relative`. |
| `priority` | Required for the LCP image (above the fold: hero, profile avatar, cover). **At most one per page.** |
| `sizes` | Required when using `fill` or when the image occupies a percentage of the viewport. |
| `placeholder` | Use `placeholder="blur"` + `blurDataURL` for remote images to prevent layout shift. |

```tsx
// ✅ Hero image — above the fold (LCP)
<Image
  src="/hero.webp"
  alt="Profile photo of Your Name, software developer"
  width={400}
  height={400}
  priority              // LCP — only on the most important image per page
  className="rounded-full"
/>

// ✅ Post cover with relative container
<div className="relative aspect-video w-full">
  <Image
    src={post.ogImageUrl}
    alt={post.title}
    fill
    sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1200px) 80vw, 760px"
    className="object-cover"
  />
</div>

// ✅ Decorative image
<Image src="/decoration.svg" alt="" width={24} height={24} aria-hidden />

// ❌ Never
<img src="/photo.jpg" alt="photo" />
```

### External domains in `next.config.ts`

If blog images come from a CDN or the backend, declare the domain in `next.config.ts`:

```ts
// apps/blog/next.config.ts
const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  images: {
    remotePatterns: [
      {
        protocol: 'https',
        hostname: 'your-cdn.com',      // replace with the real domain
        pathname: '/uploads/**',
      },
    ],
  },
};
```

