## 9. Performance and Core Web Vitals

### Fonts (`next/font`)
Fonts are already optimized with `next/font/google` and `display: 'swap'`. **Never add** additional fonts via manual `<link>` tags or `@import` in CSS.

### Third-party scripts
- Never place `<script>` tags manually in `<head>`.
- If a third-party script is needed (analytics, etc.), use `next/script` with `strategy="afterInteractive"` or `"lazyOnload"`.

```tsx
import Script from 'next/script';

// ✅ Non-blocking analytics
<Script
  src="https://analytics.example.com/script.js"
  strategy="afterInteractive"
/>
```

### Favorite song component (`apps/web`)
The component that loads the favorite song from the API **must** be a Client Component with an explicit loading state and must not block the initial page render. Reserve a fixed height to prevent CLS.

```tsx
// apps/web/app/components/FavoriteSong.tsx
'use client';

export function FavoriteSong(): React.JSX.Element {
  const { data, isLoading } = useFavoriteSong();

  // Fixed height container prevents CLS while the API call resolves
  return (
    <div className="h-16 w-full">
      {isLoading ? <FavoriteSongSkeleton /> : <SongCard song={data} />}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Animations
All CSS or Framer Motion animations must respect `prefers-reduced-motion`:

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  * { animation-duration: 0.01ms !important; transition-duration: 0.01ms !important; }
}
```

