## 10. Favicon and app icons

Place the following files in `app/` (not in `public/`). Next.js registers them automatically:

```
app/
  favicon.ico           # already exists — replace with the real one
  icon.png              # 32×32 — PNG
  apple-icon.png        # 180×180 — Apple Touch Icon
  opengraph-image.png   # 1200×630 — default OG image (social sharing fallback)
```

The `opengraph-image.png` is used as a fallback when a page does not define its own OG image. It is especially important for the portfolio. Always use `1200×630 px`.

---

## 11. Canonical URLs

The canonical URL is set via `alternates.canonical` inside the `Metadata` object. Always set it when there is a risk of duplicate URLs (pagination, query params, etc.).

```tsx
// apps/blog — home with pagination
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  alternates: {
    canonical: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL,
  },
};

// apps/blog — post detail (see section 3)
alternates: { canonical: `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/${slug}` }
```

