## 12. Pre-production checklist

### Technical
- [ ] `<html lang="es">` in both RootLayouts
- [ ] `metadataBase` points to the correct production domain per app
- [ ] `robots.ts` created in both apps
- [ ] `sitemap.ts` created in both apps (web: static, blog: dynamic)
- [ ] `generateMetadata` on every dynamic route in the blog
- [ ] `generateStaticParams` on the `[slug]` route in the blog
- [ ] JSON-LD present on web home (Person), blog home (Blog), and each post page (TechArticle)
- [ ] All images use `next/image` with `alt`, explicit dimensions, and `priority` on the LCP image
- [ ] `PostDetailMarkdown` `img` renderer uses `next/image` (not native `<img>`)
- [ ] External image domains declared in `next.config.ts` (covers both `ogImageUrl` and Markdown content images)
- [ ] `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` env var configured per app
- [ ] Default OG image (`opengraph-image.png`) present in both apps

### Content
- [ ] Unique and descriptive title per page (max 60 characters)
- [ ] Unique meta description per page (max 160 characters)
- [ ] Every post has `metaTitle`, `metaDescription`, and `ogImageUrl` filled in the admin
- [ ] Portfolio has a visible `h1` with the author's name/role
- [ ] Correct heading hierarchy (one `h1` per page)
- [ ] Post authors do not use `#` (h1) inside Markdown content — body starts at `##`

### Performance
- [ ] `priority` only on the LCP image per page
- [ ] No manual `<script>` tags in `<head>`
- [ ] Fonts loaded exclusively via `next/font`
- [ ] Favorite song component does not cause CLS
